dialect grammar
grammar stdio.pptx.diff
extension pptx
start document
comment none

# 🔺️ Real one-line `DiffCodec::print_diff`/`parse_diff` shape: `../🦀️.rs`'s `PptxDiffRecord`
# (`#[derive(dsl::DslRecord)]` with a single `value: dsl::DslValue`), printed through
# `dsl::print(.., JoinMode::Inline)` over `dsl::ToValue::to_value(self)`. The `opc=`/`presentation=`
# token form this file used to describe belonged to the hand-written `print_pptx_diff`, which the
# record derive replaced -- the printer wins, so this grammar restates the record. The payload is
# the shared, recursive `DslValue` syntax (an all-unchanged diff prints as the empty map
# `value={ }`), exactly as the sibling `🎒️zip` artifact's own diff grammar already restates it
# for the same generic codec.
document = "value" "=" REST
